</div>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unlearning Procedure.</span> From Alg. <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 4 Transformation-guided Federated Unlearning Framework ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, when a removal request is issued, the unlearning phase involves a simple fine-tuning stage on the retain set. This shows that our method helps simplify the unlearning process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span> We use two canonical datasets, CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Krizhevsky et al. (2009)</a></cite>, and the unlearning-specific dataset, MUFAC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Choi and Na (2023)</a></cite>. The client’s data distribution is sampled from a <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Dirichlet</span> distribution, with <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k,c}\sim\mathfrak{D}(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝔇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k,c}\sim\mathfrak{D}(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>, using a concentration parameter <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k,c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k,c}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the proportion of samples from class <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> assigned to client <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. For the forgetting samples, we randomly select <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30\%</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60\%</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90\%</annotation></semantics></math> of data from clients <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. For MUFAC, we use the pre-defined forget set as described in the original paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Choi and Na (2023)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics.</span> We use three metrics, including Retain Accuracy, Test Accuracy, and Membership Inference Attack Efficacy (MIA Efficacy). For MIA Efficacy, we employ the state-of-the-art (SoTA) method - LiRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Carlini et al. (2022a)</a></cite>. Details about these metrics are provided in Section <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> (Appendix).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> Regarding the FU baselines, we consider three methods: (1) <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FedEraser</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2021)</a></cite>; (2) The FU method using Projected Gradient Descent (PGD) (<span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FedPGD</span>) by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Halimi et al. (2022)</a></cite>; (3) The FU method using the AdaHessian optimizer (<span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FedAda</span>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2022)</a></cite>. To provide a comprehensive evaluation, we also include two additional baselines: an exact unlearning baseline (retrain-from-scratch), which is the gold standard of unlearning, and a decentralized adaptation of an MU method that employs <math id="S5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-sparsification followed by fine-tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024a)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation.</span> In the collaborative learning stage, we conduct the FL simulations over <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=50</annotation></semantics></math> communication rounds for <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10</annotation></semantics></math> clients’ models.
The unlearning stage applies FU methods for <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and the number of local epochs is set to <math id="S5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>. More implementation details are provided in Section <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> (Appendix).</p>
</div>
