<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix for ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems
Forget User Data</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides supplementary materials to support the main paper. It includes detailed proofs for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Transformation Composition for Improving Unlearning Performance ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S3.E5" title="In Corollary 1. ‣ 3.2 Transformation Composition for Improving Unlearning Performance ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> (Section <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proofs ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>), additional empirical results on the CIFAR-10 dataset demonstrating the effectiveness of transformation-guided unlearning (Section <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B More Experiments on CIFAR-10 ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>), implementation details (Section <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>), transformations details (Section <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Details of Applied Transformations ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>), and more discussion on the relationship between transformation intensity and unlearning performance from the lens of sample difficulty using the relative Mahalanobis distance (Section <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Additional Discussion ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Transformation Composition for Improving Unlearning Performance ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> on Transformation Composition for Unlearning</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the first inequality: <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4. ‣ 3.1 Unlearning Optimization Problem ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the mutual information <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta,\theta^{\prime};D_{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta,\theta^{\prime};D_{S})</annotation></semantics></math> measures the amount of information is shared between models parameterized by <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to dataset <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined using the KL divergence:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(\theta,\theta^{\prime};D_{S})=D_{KL}(p_{\theta,\theta^{\prime}}(x,y)\|p_{\theta}(x|y)p_{\theta^{\prime}}(y|x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta,\theta^{\prime};D_{S})=D_{KL}(p_{\theta,\theta^{\prime}}(x,y)\|p_{\theta}(x|y)p_{\theta^{\prime}}(y|x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{KL}(p_{\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1}}(x,y)\parallel p_{\theta}(x|y)p_{\mathcal{T}_{1}}(y|x))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{KL}(p_{\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1}}(x,y)\parallel p_{\theta}(x|y)p_{\mathcal{T}_{1}}(y|x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{1}\circ\mathcal{T}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{1}\circ\mathcal{T}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> which means <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}(\theta)=\mathcal{T}_{2}(\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}(\theta)=\mathcal{T}_{2}(\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta)),</annotation></semantics></math> we also have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{KL}(p_{\theta,T^{\prime 2}}(x,y)\parallel p_{\theta}(x|y)p_{T^{\prime 2}}(y|x))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{KL}(p_{\theta,T^{\prime 2}}(x,y)\parallel p_{\theta}(x|y)p_{T^{\prime 2}}(y|x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To establish the inequality, we leverage the data processing inequality for mutual information <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover (1999)</a></cite>. Consider the Markov chain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta)\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{2}(\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta))=T^{\prime(2)}(\theta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta)\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{2}(\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta))=T^{\prime(2)}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">This Markov structure is justified because <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> operates solely on <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and has no direct access to <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of function composition, any information flow from <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> must pass through <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. The data processing inequality states that for any Markov chain <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\rightarrow Y\rightarrow Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\rightarrow Y\rightarrow Z</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;Z)\leq I(X;Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;Z)\leq I(X;Y)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover (1999)</a></cite>. Applying this to our context, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}(\theta);D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta);D_{forget})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)}(\theta);D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1}(\theta);D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is designed to reduce information about <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime\prime}_{forget}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime\prime}_{forget}</annotation></semantics></math> in the model, and the mutual information is evaluated with respect to samples from <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{forget}=D^{\prime}_{forget}\cup D^{\prime\prime}_{forget}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{forget}=D^{\prime}_{forget}\cup D^{\prime\prime}_{forget}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">A similar argument applies for the second inequality <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{2};D_{forget})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{\prime(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{2};D_{forget})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For inequalities 3 and 4 regarding <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{2}\circ\mathcal{T}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{2}\circ\mathcal{T}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we establish the Markov chain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\theta\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{2}(\theta)\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{1}(\mathcal{T}_{2}(\theta))=\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)}(\theta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{2}(\theta)\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{1}(\mathcal{T}_{2}(\theta))=\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the data processing inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)};D_{forget})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)};D_{forget})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{2};D_{forget})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{2};D_{forget}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)};D_{forget})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{{}^{\prime\prime}(2)};D_{forget})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{1};D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof of all four inequalities in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Transformation Composition for Improving Unlearning Performance ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#S3.E5" title="In Corollary 1. ‣ 3.2 Transformation Composition for Improving Unlearning Performance ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> on Monotonic Unlearning Performance</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The corollary follows by induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">For the base two-transformation case (<math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>):<span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
From Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Transformation Composition for Improving Unlearning Performance ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we know that when <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{1}\circ\mathcal{T}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{1}\circ\mathcal{T}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(1)}=\mathcal{T}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(1)}=\mathcal{T}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(1)};D_{forget})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(1)};D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, when <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{2}\circ\mathcal{T}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(2)}=\mathcal{T}_{2}\circ\mathcal{T}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(1)}=\mathcal{T}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(1)}=\mathcal{T}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(1)};D_{forget})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(2)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(1)};D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">For the generalized design of multi-transformation case <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">:
Let <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(m+1)}=\mathcal{T}_{{}_{m+1}}\circ\mathcal{T}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(m+1)}=\mathcal{T}_{{}_{m+1}}\circ\mathcal{T}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{{m+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{{m+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an additional transformation designed to unlearn some aspect of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{forget}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{forget}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the Markov chain: <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\rightarrow\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta)\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{{m+1}}(\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\rightarrow\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta)\rightarrow\mathcal{T}_{{m+1}}(\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta))</annotation></semantics></math>, by the data processing inequality from information theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover (1999)</a></cite>, we know that:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{{m+1}}(\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta));D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta);D_{forget})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\theta,\mathcal{T}_{{m+1}}(\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta));D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m)}(\theta);D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">This gives us:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m+1)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m)};D_{forget})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m+1)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m)};D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by the principle of induction, we have the following inequality for any <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m-1)};D_{forget})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m)};D_{forget})\leq I(\theta,\mathcal{T}^{(m-1)};D_{forget}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>More Experiments on CIFAR-10</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide additional empirical results on the CIFAR-10 dataset to complement the analysis presented in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Empirical Validation of Transformation Effects ‣ 3 Theoretical and Empirical Analysis: Unlearning from the Lens of Transformation ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. Figure <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix B More Experiments on CIFAR-10 ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> illustrates these findings.
Figures <a href="#A2.F6.sf1" title="In Figure 6 ‣ Appendix B More Experiments on CIFAR-10 ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6a</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F6.sf3" title="In Figure 6 ‣ Appendix B More Experiments on CIFAR-10 ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6c</span></a> show examples of forgetting samples subjected to increasing transformation intensity via progressive augmentation and masking, respectively.
The corresponding plots in Figures <a href="#A2.F6.sf2" title="In Figure 6 ‣ Appendix B More Experiments on CIFAR-10 ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6b</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F6.sf4" title="In Figure 6 ‣ Appendix B More Experiments on CIFAR-10 ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6d</span></a> demonstrate a strong positive correlation between the applied transformation intensity and the overall federated unlearning (FU) performance. These results on CIFAR-10 mirror those observed for CIFAR-100, further substantiating the relationship between increased transformation intensity and improved unlearning effectiveness explored in our work.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15861v1/progressive_transform_illustration_CIFAR10.png" id="A2.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/59;" width="429" height="59" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Increasing intensity level of transformation applied to forgetting samples.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15861v1/progressive_transform_CIFAR10.svg" id="A2.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/290;" width="429" height="290"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Increasing masking ratio applied to forgetting samples.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15861v1/progressive_masking_illustration_CIFAR10.png" id="A2.F6.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/59;" width="429" height="59" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Overall unlearning performance improves when increasing the intensity level of transformation on the forgetting samples.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15861v1/progressive_masking_CIFAR10.svg" id="A2.F6.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/289;" width="429" height="289"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>Overall unlearning performance improves when increasing the intensity level of transformation on the forgetting samples.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Experiments on CIFAR-10 show that the unlearning process becomes more effective when models learn from transformed
sample. (Two Top) Progressive Transformation and (Two Bottom) Progressive Masking. The top figures present forgetting samples with increasing intensity level, while the bottom figures illustrate the correlation between unlearning performance and the intensity level of transformation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics.</span> Three metrics used to evaluate our ToFU framework include:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Retain Accuracy</span>: Measures the unlearned model’s performance on the retain sets, calculated as the average accuracy across all client retain sets (<math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Test Accuracy</span>: Evaluates the unlearned model’s generalization capability on an unseen test set.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Membership Inference Attack Efficacy (MIA Efficacy)</span>: A privacy-focused metric evaluates the success of an unlearning request by determining whether attackers can distinguish forgotten examples from unseen ones. It is defined as the ratio of samples in the forget set that are correctly estimated as non-training samples. Regarding the MIA model, we employ the state-of-the-art method LiRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Carlini et al. (2022a)</a></cite>. The shadow models are constructed by using the global model parameters from the final 5 communication rounds of the FL training process.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Local models, ResNet-18 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al. (2016)</a></cite>, are trained for <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> epochs using Schedule-free-AdamW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Defazio et al. (2024)</a></cite> optimizer (batch size <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=128</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=3\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=3\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments were conducted on a system equipped with two NVIDIA RTX 4090 GPUs, an AMD EPYC 9654P CPU, and 192GB of RAM. Our codebase is developed using PyTorch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al. (2019)</a></cite> and the Flower <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Beutel et al. (2020)</a></cite> federated learning framework.
For each client dataset, we reserve 10% of the client data for validation purposes, ensuring that the validation set reflects the client’s local data distribution. Key hyperparameters for the transformations used within the ToFU framework are detailed in Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Hyperparameters for Transformations used in ToFU.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
