          <span id="algorithm2.6.15.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Color transforms </span><math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\{\mathcal{T}_{2},\mathcal{T}_{3},\mathcal{T}_{5}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\{\mathcal{T}_{2},\mathcal{T}_{3},\mathcal{T}_{5}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span id="algorithm2.6.15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"><math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Color space alterations</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">13</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm2.6.16.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Noise/Blur transforms </span><math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\{\mathcal{T}_{4},\mathcal{T}_{6},\mathcal{T}_{8}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">8</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\{\mathcal{T}_{4},\mathcal{T}_{6},\mathcal{T}_{8}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span id="algorithm2.6.16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"><math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Information degradation</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">14</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm2.6.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Progressive transformation:</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">15</span></span>
          <math id="algorithm2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}\leftarrow\min(m,8)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">8</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}\leftarrow\min(m,8)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.18.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span id="algorithm2.6.18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"><math id="algorithm2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Bound intensity level</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">16</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm2.6.19.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">selected_transforms </span><math id="algorithm2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.19.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> TRANSFORMS</span><math id="algorithm2.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0:m^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0:m^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.19.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span id="algorithm2.6.19.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"><math id="algorithm2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.19.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Take first <math id="algorithm2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> transforms</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">17</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm2.6.20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="algorithm2.6.20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><em id="algorithm2.6.20.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Compose(selected_transforms)</em><span id="algorithm2.6.20.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span id="algorithm2.6.20.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"><math id="algorithm2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.20.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Apply sequentially</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.21" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Details of Applied Transformations</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#algorithm2" title="In Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents transformations used in our experiments. These transformations are implemented using the <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">albumentation</span> library.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Additional Ablation Study</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Ablation study on transformation-invariant regularize strength</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct an ablation study (Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ E.1 Ablation study on transformation-invariant regularize strength ‣ Appendix E Additional Ablation Study ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) on the CIFAR-10 dataset to analyze further the impact of the transformation-invariant regularizer strength, controlled by the hyperparameter <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S4.E6" title="In 4 Transformation-guided Federated Unlearning Framework ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), on ToFU’s performance. We observe that <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., removing the regularizer) leads to reasonable performance. However, introducing a small positive regularization (<math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) slightly improves the overall performance. This suggests that encouraging the model to learn consistent representations across transformations is beneficial. Conversely, setting <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=-1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=-1.0</annotation></semantics></math> drastically degrades performance across all metrics. This is expected, as a negative <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> effectively maximizes the KL divergence in Eq. <a href="#S4.E6" title="In 4 Transformation-guided Federated Unlearning Framework ‣ ToFU: Transforming How Federated Learning Systems Forget User Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, forcing the representations of original and transformed samples to diverge, which hinders learning. Increasing <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to higher positive values (<math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=2.0</annotation></semantics></math>) maintains high utility but slightly reduces the MIA Efficacy and the overall score compared to the optimal range. These findings support our choice of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.01</annotation></semantics></math> in the main experiments as a default, although fine-tuning <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., to 0.5 for CIFAR-10) can yield marginal improvements.</p>
</div>
